   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["num_cols = ['electricity_kwh', 'fuel_liters', 'travel_km_day', 'waste_kg_week', 'carbon_score']\nsns.pairplot(df[num_cols].dropna(), diag_kind='kde', plot_kws={'alpha': 0.3, 's': 15},\n            diag_kws={'fill': True})\nplt.suptitle('Pairplot â€” Numerical Features', y=1.02, fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\nplt.show()"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 9. Observations\n\n- The dataset contains **1,500 household records** with 9 features and 1 target variable (`carbon_score`).\n- Approximately **3% missing values** exist in numerical columns â€” handled via median imputation.\n- The `carbon_score` ranges from ~100 to ~1,200 kg COâ‚‚/month with a mean around **550 kg COâ‚‚/month**.\n- `electricity_kwh`, `fuel_liters`, and `travel_km_day` show strong positive correlation with `carbon_score`.\n- **Petrol** and **Diesel** vehicle users show significantly higher carbon scores.\n- **Meat-heavy** food habits show the highest average carbon scores among dietary categories.\n\n---\nâœ… **Data Understanding Complete. Proceed to `preprocessing.ipynb`.**"]
  }
 ]
